#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:2 93d33af544a547d0baaf84e5e8c2dd2a
msgid "Adopting a tape that is already on disk"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:4 872815ed7a9e4557b88b723e5ad73fd4
msgid ""
"A tape's data outlives the library that held it. Removing a library "
"leaves its cartridges under ``/opt/mhvtl``, and *adopting* one puts it "
"into a library again, with everything that was written to it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:13 f917e6069722415092e8c0999409629c
msgid "When this comes up"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:15 1b359b03c6fb4067a1b078ca6bfec3ae
msgid "A library was removed without ``--remove-media`` - the usual case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:16 75353411624346de9c253b956e7670c6
msgid ""
"A library was rebuilt, because MHVTL reads its vendor and model once and "
"changing them means recreating it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:18 fd61e044b5fd497e8221fabb652ff893
msgid "Tape files were copied from another host."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:21 b6a1e6fc7dd846ed9f2adc678bbee83f
msgid "Finding them"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:34 0beec9ff576142808c90f2bf0a586238
msgid ""
"Orphaned tapes are listed apart from everything else the console "
"considers orphaned, and are never cleaned up automatically. They are "
"data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:38 781863d927ac49c49b968c0df2d8d1f1
msgid "Adopting one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:40 28d4f441232e4bf1af089002e23cafc1
msgid ""
"**Tapes → Inventory**, then **Adopt**, or on the operator's tape pages. "
"The list offers the tapes on disk that no library lists, and the "
"libraries whose drives can read that generation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:44 dccdaa4f1c1b4401a87bf1901cba3e99
msgid "Tapes on disk with no library, each with an Adopt button"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:57 edfbcfea58ab480daee7770aa1e83946
msgid "Only the libraries that could load it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:59 78016024d208408bad73a5c78006cc08
msgid ""
"The dropdown beside each tape lists **only the libraries whose drives can"
" load that cartridge**, not every library on the host. A Sony library "
"with AIT drives is not offered for an LTO-7 tape, because it could never "
"read it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:63 8ce21dfe0b1947b1b968660bcadccec0
msgid ""
"The command line draws the same line, and when it refuses it says where "
"the tape *could* go rather than leaving you to try the libraries one at a"
" time:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:73 2431a9cce5b246f696b2ee130e68cb92
msgid ""
"**Loads, not writes.** The test is whether a drive can *read* the "
"cartridge, which is looser than whether it can write one. An LTO-7 drive "
"reads LTO-5, so a library whose newest drive is an LTO-7 is offered for "
"an LTO-5 tape - and it should be, because adopting recovers what is "
"already on a tape rather than writing to it. A library offered here may "
"still refuse to *create* a new cartridge of that generation; see :ref"
":`mixed-libraries`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:80 ba90c004d7474c0eae7ecb1fdf2b3a8d
msgid ""
"If a tape is offered nowhere, the row says so instead of showing an empty"
" dropdown, and the reason is the same one the command prints. Adding a "
"drive that can read it changes the answer immediately - no library has to"
" be rebuilt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:86 afef2e647e224dd1ac4c520a4441470e
msgid "What it does, and what it does not"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:88 7c4142f5f550457dbcdda5710244f5f5
msgid ""
"It adds the cartridge to ``library_contents.50`` and leaves its files "
"exactly where they are. Nothing is copied, nothing is rewritten, and the "
"data is not read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:92 1646df68f98c4e54a6792d8225d5734d
msgid ""
"The library must have a free slot, and its drives must take that "
"generation - an LTO-8 cartridge cannot be adopted into a library of AIT "
"drives, because nothing there could ever load it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:97 a3fe18fa7e874f74960e8d8cc5aab809
msgid "Restart the library afterwards"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:99 75c6ea7164c24d87aba1d3780edaf3f3
msgid ""
"MHVTL reads ``library_contents`` once, when the library starts, so its "
"robot does not see the adopted tape until it restarts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:106 03fde1ba5c5b4a408584f0d29e69c139
msgid ""
"Both the console and the command line say this after an adopt, and the "
"library page flags a library whose configuration and robot disagree."
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:110 387c05739be24bb6941e153626b810ba
msgid "Checking the data survived"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:112 9d79963f7e05424995128b191c3855cf
msgid "Mount it and ask the drive:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../tapes/adopt.rst:123 d213ebe254364276bc83f85d4d40deee
msgid ""
"A tape that kept its data reports what was written to it. One that lost "
"its files reports an empty cartridge - and ``mhvtl tape list`` would have"
" said ``ON DISK: no`` before you mounted it."
msgstr ""

